          "p42 4261",
          "p43 4261"
        ],
        "stays": [
          "p14 3707",
          "p15 3707"
        ]
      },
      {
        "does": "Rolling the buggy works the engine's piston: a pin in the 24-tooth gear on the left rear axle is a crank, and a connecting rod pushes the piston up and down in its block behind the seat.",
        "mechanisms": [
          "piston-engine: 1 cylinder"
        ],
        "source": "book: steps 3-5 (the inset in step 4 shows the pin in the gear); that rolling drives it is inferred, as the gear only sits on the left rear axle",
        "control": "p700 3482",
        "moves": [
          "p20 3648a",
          "p25 3652"
        ]
      },
      {
        "does": "The front wheels turn freely on pins in the steering arms.",
        "mechanisms": [
          "free-wheels"
        ],
        "source": "book: steps 5 and 15",
        "control": [
          "p698 3482",
          "p701 3482"
        ]
      },
      {
        "does": "The rear wheels are on two separate axles; only the left one turns the engine.",
        "mechanisms": [
          "free-wheels"
        ],
        "source": "book: steps 2 and 15",
        "control": [
          "p699 3482",
          "p700 3482"
        ],
        "note": "inferred: the right rear axle turns on its own and drives nothing"
      },
      {
        "does": "The roll cage, the seat and the steering column's mounting stay rigid: the toothed toggle joints hold their angle, and the cage is a closed frame.",
        "mechanisms": [
          "rigid"
        ],
        "source": "inferred: steps 10-14 build the cage from toothed toggle joints, which click and hold, and the seat folds round its hinge axle only while it is built",
